{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "day": 17,
  "level": 2,
  "title": { "en": "21 to 50", "es": "Del veintiuno al cincuenta" },
  "objectives": [
    "Count from 21 to 29 as single words",
    "Build 31 to 50 with tens + y + units",
    "Ask ¿Cuántos? and ¿Cuántas? about how many"
  ],
  "teach": [
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**21 to 29 are written as one word.** Take *veinte*, swap the final -e for **-i**, and add the unit:\n\n- veinte → **veinti**uno, **veinti**dós, **veinti**trés\n- veinticuatro, veinticinco, **veintiséis**, veintisiete, veintiocho, veintinueve\n\nThree of them take an accent: **veintidós**, **veintitrés**, **veintiséis**."
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "veintiuno, veintidós, veintitrés", "en": "21, 22, 23" },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**From 31 on, it's tens + y + units**, written as three words:\n\n- **treinta** (30) → **treinta y uno**, treinta y dos…\n- **cuarenta** (40) → cuarenta y cinco…\n- **cincuenta** (50)\n\nThe *y* is said quickly, joined to the words around it: *treinta-y-uno*."
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "treinta y uno, cuarenta, cincuenta", "en": "31, 40, 50", "note": "Cuarenta and cincuenta both start with the cu- of cuatro and cinco." },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "Before a masculine noun, **uno** shortens: *veintiún euros*, *treinta y un euros*. Before a feminine noun it becomes **una**: *veintiuna cervezas*. On its own, counting, it stays **uno**."
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Cuántos?", "en": "How many?", "note": "It agrees with the noun: ¿Cuántos amigos? (m) / ¿Cuántas cañas? (f). ¿Cuánto es? asks the price, which is a different question." }
  ],
  "vocab": [
    { "id": "veintiuno", "es": "veintiuno", "en": "twenty-one", "pos": "num", "ipa": "beintiˈuno", "note": "veintiún before a masculine noun: veintiún euros." },
    { "id": "veintidos", "es": "veintidós", "en": "twenty-two", "pos": "num", "ipa": "beintiˈðos" },
    { "id": "veintitres", "es": "veintitrés", "en": "twenty-three", "pos": "num", "ipa": "beintiˈtɾes" },
